["<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa794b8292681616c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_018vvjEummgtE6GSAJWSweBU</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/88da6e5c-69d1-4aa0-b4ec-646181c19911/tasks/aa794b8292681616c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Opus designs skill/stat core method\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've revised both files against the second research note, and every 〔待二稿〕 marker is resolved. The only one left is in the title of §9, which is the table recording how each was handled. Nothing is committed; I only merged main into the worktree.\n\n**What changed from the first draft:**\n1. **The common unit E is now only a screening tool.** It flags the most suspicious skills to test next; it no longer claims anything is balanced. §1.4 lists what it can't see: readability, whether a skill makes boss mechanics pointless, multiple targets, combo blow-ups, player skill level, feel, and the fact that fights are won at a threshold rather than linearly.\n2. **Each skill is now recorded as an action timeline first.** That means wind-up, active time, recovery and which part a dash can cancel, defence, range, hits, posture and proc coefficient. A new window check asks whether each skill fits inside the boss's reaction or punish window. Time cost now counts only the part that can't be cancelled, and is zero while the boss is mid-attack, since the player would be dodging then anyway.\n3. **That check changed conclusions:**\n   - **Parry:** after seeing the boss's red flash, the player can only reach about 0.15 s of the 0.20 s window. If the success rate comes in under 70%, widen the window first; don't add reward.\n   - **Heavy strike:** with its recovery dash-cancellable, it becomes 31 damage plus 69 posture, instead of 47 plus 53. In phase 2 it only has 0.25 s to spare.\n   - **Thrust:** 36 damage drops to 27, and against charge it is now \"can counter, depending on distance\" rather than a hard counter.\n   - I also corrected an error: the charge ends about 14 − d₀ m from the player (d₀ = their distance when it starts), not a fixed 14 m. That means charge is only reliably hard-countered by the companion's ranged attacks, and once the companion dies that counter is gone.\n4. **Four new rules:**\n   - **Proc coefficients** on every hit of every skill, plus a lint check.\n   - **Damage-multiplier audit.** dash_strike, last_stand and late_retort are each a separate multiplier, stacking to 2.81× and 4.2× during a posture break. This is the same pattern Diablo IV 1.2 fixed.\n   - **A 5-step validation process** replaces win-rate thresholds. It adds a fixed-boss-sequence test mode and a \"record hits but don't apply damage\" mode.\n   - **\"Function over % damage\" check for talents.** Route Minor nodes should enlarge their own route's effect instead of adding generic stats. Weak crit nodes should get a new behaviour rather than bigger numbers.\n5. **Posture values stay placeholders** (120 full bar, 100 single-skill cap, the posture value), each with a calibration order. The posture bar is listed as a must-be-visible UI item.\n6. **Unchanged:** all of the user's decisions in core-skills §16, and \"parry + heavy strike first\" for M1.\n\n**Decisions for the user (defaults in brackets):**\n- **U1, cooldown rhythm:** parry 6 s, thrust 8 s, heavy strike 8 s, guard 12 s.\n- **U2, how much skills add over basic attacks:** 50%, so skills are about a third of the player's damage. This only moves the screening line.\n- **U3, can one skill break a full posture bar:** no, a single skill does at most 100 of 120. The ice seal + heavy strike combo can break it.\n- **U4, knight skill keys:** K/L/U/O, with core-skills' Q/E/R/F as the alternative. I opens the bag in combat and sits between U and O, so ask about misfires.\n- **U5, damage multipliers:** fold all conditional damage bonuses into the additive pool, keeping only crit and posture-break damage as separate multipliers. late_retort becomes +50% / −30% and last_stand becomes +25%, both additive.\n\n**Open questions with defaults:**\n- **Q1:** keep adaptive pacing inside boss fights, which is the opposite of Left 4 Dead. Default: keep it, but it may only swap moves within the threat band.\n- **Q2:** how to count the combo damage share. Counting only the hit that uses up the state gives 23%; counting the whole chain gives 83%. The target band is 25–35%. Default: count only that hit.\n- **Q3:** whether to give the knight a counter to charge for after the companion dies. Default: measure first, don't add one.\n- **Q4:** mine field is the weakest move, with a single weak counter. Default: accept it as a move whose job is reading dodge habits.\n\nFiles are in /Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/design-method/docs/proposals/:\n- design-method.md\n- design-method-tables.md (two new tables: T4 damage-multiplier audit, T5 skill timelines and window checks)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>308071</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>14</tool_uses><duration_ms>302035</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "常规的验收还是用subagent(sonnet)模型做的"]
